Request the shader-f16 WebGPU feature when the adapter has it, so fp16 ONNX
models (half the size of fp32, faster) run in the ONNX Image Model node.
Without it Dawn rejects every f16 compute pipeline ("Invalid ComputePipeline
Cast"). initGPU already drops features the adapter lacks, so this is safe on
adapters without f16.

--- a/src/figment.js
+++ b/src/figment.js
@@ export async function initGPU(options = {}) {
-  const { requiredFeatures = [], requiredLimits = {}, powerPreference = 'high-performance' } = options;
+  const { requiredFeatures = ['shader-f16'], requiredLimits = {}, powerPreference = 'high-performance' } = options;
